@@ -21750,3 +21750,22 @@ Direct follow-up to patch 0270's separate-icon-vs-banner split and patch 0273's
 **The actual image files are NOT part of this patch**, same reasoning as patch 0273's icon delivery: binary art doesn't belong in a text diff. Delivered separately as two ready-to-drop folders -- 30 `<chain_id>.png` files for `public/lore/chains/`, 8 `<raid_id>.png` files for `public/lore/raids/`. Once those land, every chain and raid's banner should resolve immediately in both the collapsed-card view (still showing the dedicated `icon` from patch 0273 where assigned) and the detail-modal/active-raid views (which always show this full `banner`, per patch 0270's own split).
 
 **Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and a full `vite build` (both Electron sub-builds included) pass clean.
+
+### Quest tag banners + icons -- all 6 tags wired to real dedicated art (patch 0275)
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Quest Tag Art
+
+- All 6 quest tags (Combat, Escort, Explore, Arcane, Stealth, Defense) now have real dedicated banner and icon art
+```
+
+Direct follow-up to patch 0270's icon-vs-banner split: real art for all 6 quest tags, delivered as 6 individual full-size banner files plus one labeled icon reference sheet.
+
+**Banners came pre-generated as individual files this time**, each built around a decorative diamond "medallion" bookend on the left and a matching flag/pole bookend on the right, with the actual scene filling the middle. Direct request: keep those bookend symbols out of focus, centered composition preferred. Since both bookends only occupy the outer ~250px on either side of each 1230x212 source image, a plain center crop to the target 636x212 (3:1) naturally lands entirely within the clean scene in the middle -- verified visually against all 6 before use, no bookend bleed into any of them.
+
+**Icons came as one labeled 3x2 reference sheet** (same format as previous DevTools-sourced sheets), cropped and matched to its printed label directly, no order-guessing needed.
+
+**`quest-tags.json`: every tag's `banner.path` now points at the new art**, `quest-tags/<id>.png` -- already the correct convention on disk before this patch (same story as quest chains in patch 0274), but the old `focusX`/`focusY`/`scale` values were tuned for completely different placeholder art and no longer meant anything sensible against the new center-cropped images, so those got reset to unset/default (plain centered cover) rather than carried over. **Every tag's `icon.path`** (unset since patch 0270 introduced the field) now points at `quest-tags-icons/<id>.png`, matching the same folder convention `defaultFolder` already used for its id-guess fallback.
+
+**The actual image files are NOT part of this patch**, same reasoning as every other art-delivery patch here. Delivered separately as two ready-to-drop folders -- 6 `<tag_id>.png` banner files for `public/lore/quest-tags/`, 6 `<tag_id>.png` icon files for `public/lore/quest-tags-icons/`.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and a full `vite build` (both Electron sub-builds included) pass clean.
